-- A NAMED-FIELD VARIANT: the registry key is `Dup`, the type is `RA`.  That gap is what
-- sends `mkA.dx` down the field->owners fallback instead of the exact
-- `lookupRecordByName <head tycon>` hit, and it is why this shape is not covered by any
-- cell built out of short-form records.
--
-- ⚠️ `dpre` IS NOT PADDING — it puts `dx` at OFFSET 1 here while `wmod`'s rival owner
-- puts it at offset 0, so a wrong pick between the two is a wrong VALUE (`99` instead of
-- `7`) and not merely a diagnostic.  A single-field version of this record cannot express
-- that: both layouts would pick index 0 and the wrong pick would be invisible on the
-- executed binary, which is exactly how #1382 shipped past `diff_compiler_engines`.
-- (#1455 adversarial review, finding 2 — the body's "every new fixture uses records with
-- >=2 differently-ordered fields" claim was false of this cell and its sibling.)
public export data RA =
  | Dup { dpre : Int, dx : Int }
  | ACount Int

export mkA : RA
mkA = Dup { dpre = 99, dx = 7 }
